        "summary": "hypothesis=Cross-payer pattern CONFIRMED on second neonatal case in cohort: warmer charges + monitor charges are deducted in full as non-admissibles on NICU/PICU neonatal claims. First observed on case_dadcf280fbd7 (Paramount/NIC NICU sepsis): warmer Rs.48,000 + monitor Rs.8,400 fully deducted. Now confirmed on case_25b13fb504d7 (Medi Assist/Manipal Cigna NICU late-preterm RDS): warmer Rs.9,000 + monitor Rs.2,500 fully deducted. Two different payers across two different policy/corporate combinations show the same structural deduction of warmer + monitor as non-payable for NICU stays. This is likely policy-wide IRDAI guidance or industry-standard non-payable list for neonatal care. Recoverable lever for Jyothi: (a) recognise that warmer + monitor charges on NICU/PICU bills are NOT recoverable from insurer and must be either (i) collected from family, (ii) absorbed by hospital, or (iii) NOT billed separately in the first place (built into NICU package rate); (b) audit whether family-payment collection on these line items happens consistently — if uncollected, hospital absorbs more than the discount alone implies; (c) consider repositioning these charges as bundled into the NICU per-day rate for future claims where the negotiated package permits. Cry-wolf guarded; does NOT feed tier1_recoverable.; tier=3",
