        "summary": "hypothesis=CITI Scans & Diagnostics (Jyothi's external lab partner) recorded this neonatal patient's gender INCORRECTLY as 'Male' on the first two of three lab invoices (31-May-2025 CBC/CRP/Calcium/Electrolytes; 02-Jun-2025 Bilirubin/Blood-Group/TSH). The third invoice (04-Jun-2025 Serum Bilirubin Total) has the gender CORRECTED to 'Female'. The same patient_aadhaar and same Req-No-pattern flow through all three; only the gender field flipped. Likely cause: CITI Scans's order-entry system defaults gender = Male and the first two requisitions were entered without correction. On a newborn referral pattern (where the baby is identified as 'Baby Of <maternal name>' rather than by own name), the operator may have skipped the gender field. Clinical impact on this case is NIL — all six tests (CBC, CRP, Calcium, Electrolytes, Bilirubin, TSH, Blood Group, Serum Bilirubin Total) are sex-neutral with no gender-dependent reference ranges or interpretation. But the same lab's process-quality issue is a latent risk for tests where reference ranges differ by sex (e.g. testosterone, BMD, certain hormone panels). Process-quality observation; not a billing concern. The hospital may wish to raise this with CITI Scans operationally. Cry-wolf guarded; does NOT feed tier1_recoverable.; tier=3",
