        "summary": "hypothesis=Time-based PICU-rate items (PICU bed, oxygen, warmer, monitor) billed at 12X uniformly across the stay, but clinical evidence supports differential billing: (a) case sheet annotation shows day-1 (~20 hours, 27/05 17:00 - 28/05 13:00) was in general room 305, not PICU; (b) discharge summary narrative states patient was 'shifted out of NICU on day 9' with 'afebrile period of over 6 days' before discharge. Paramount's deduction model partly catches this — warmer charges Rs.48,000 deducted entirely as not payable, monitor charges Rs.8,400 deducted entirely — but the bigger structural issue is whether the hospital should have billed day-1 at a lower regular-room rate AND/OR whether the high-acuity (PICU/oxygen/warmer) charges should have stopped at day-9 when the patient was clinically out of NICU. Recoverable lever if pattern recurs: (1) tighter alignment of billing days to clinical-record care intensity, especially for items that the payer deducts as 'not payable' (e.g. warmer); (2) explicit step-down rate structure for post-NICU recovery days. Hypothesis to test across the remaining neonatal/NICU cases in cohort.; tier=3",
