        "summary": "hypothesis=Vidal/Oriental corporate GMC deduction model on this case is a 3-component structure: (1) universal ~10% MoU discount on bill total (Rs.5,472 = 9.998% of Rs.54,715; hospital-absorbed with explicit 'do not collect' annotation); (2) itemised non-admissibles (Rs.3,370 = monitor remaining 90% + medicine consumables; patient-collectible); (3) ~10% copay on pre-copay admissible (Rs.4,587 = 10% × Rs.45,873; patient-collectible per policy T&C). NO tariff-excess component. This is structurally the Paramount 4-component model MINUS the tariff-excess line. Total non-paid Rs.13,429 = 24.5% of bill, split insurer-pays-93.2%-of-authorised vs hospital-absorbs-Rs.5,472 vs patient-pays-Rs.7,957. Across the cohort's 5 deduction models so far (FHPL bucketed-absorption, Bajaj retail itemised-collectible, Bajaj corporate hybrid, Paramount complex-4-component, Vidal/Oriental discount-plus-non-admissibles-plus-copay), the recoverable-lever profile differs per model and per payer; cohort-level patterns will become clearer past ~10 cases. Cry-wolf guarded; does NOT feed tier1_recoverable. Feeds payer_profile_store.; tier=3",
