        "source_artifact_file": null,
        "summary": "hypothesis=Refinement to the clinical/billing doctor-attribution pattern observed across cohort cases. Previously hypothesised (from case_125375275679 e012): Jyothi shows a clinical/billing doctor split where the billing record carries the visiting-surgeon name and the clinical record carries a letterhead-consultant name. This case (an LSCS by Dr. M. Durgadevi, same visiting surgeon as the comparator case's LSCS) shows NO SPLIT — Durgadevi appears as treating doctor across ALL artefacts (case sheet, DS, Part B, pre-auth, bill header). Same surgeon as the comparator case's case, but consistent attribution across all artefacts here. Comparing the three relevant cases: (1) case_f90295b5e3c2 the comparator case LSCS — clinical=Sunitha (consultant of record on case sheet header), billing=Durgadevi (on pre-auth, bill, Part B). SPLIT. (2) case_125375275679 multi-lipoma — clinical=Gopala Rao (case sheet, DS, Part B, pre-auth), billing=Anil Kumar (only on bill header). SPLIT. (3) THIS CASE LSCS — clinical=Durgadevi, billing=Durgadevi. NO SPLIT. Refined hypothesis: the split is NOT a Jyothi-wide convention but case-specific based on whether the inpatient management is led by a different specialist than the procedural surgeon. On the comparator case, Sunitha (DCH/DMCH paediatric+maternal medicine) led pre/post-op management; on this case, Durgadevi may have been the consultant of record throughout (no separate DCH/DMCH consultant assigned). The split is a marker of MULTI-SPECIALIST CASE MANAGEMENT, not a default billing convention. Cohort lens: when measuring revenue per doctor, the split-case bills attribute revenue to the surgeon-only; the no-split-case bills attribute to the consultant-of-record-throughout. For accurate doctor-level revenue analysis, the split needs to be detected per-case (compare case sheet header vs bill header — agreement = no split, disagreement = split). Pattern hardness: 2 splits in 3 surgical cases observed (66%). Not a small-N effect; merits being a tier-3 cohort tracking item.; tier=3",
