          "rate_structure_vs_comparator_lscs_note": "Same payer (NIA), same TPA (FHPL), same corporate policy (Apitoria GMP), same procedure (LSCS), same hospital, same room category (Single A/C) — but per-day and per-line rates differ between the comparator case and this case. THIS case: Room Rs.2500/day, Consultant Rs.1500/day, Nursing Rs.800/day, Surgeon Rs.16,000, Anaesthesia Rs.4,000, OT Rs.4,000, Assistant Rs.5,000... actually Assistant Rs.4,000 here. the comparator case: Room Rs.2000/day, Consultant Rs.1000/day, Nursing Rs.800/day, Surgeon Rs.15,000, Anaesthesia Rs.5,000, OT Rs.5,000, Assistant Rs.5,000. Differentials: Room +25%, Consultant +50%, Nursing 0%, Surgeon +6.7%, Anaesthesia -20%, OT -20%, Assistant -20%. Net effect on total: Rs.59,488 vs Rs.56,853 (+4.6%). Differential rate sheets — or rate-card-by-doctor (different per-line rates by which surgeon/anaesthetist was on the case) — could explain. The total falls within the NIA/FHPL tariff cap (which appears to be ~Rs.35,000-40,000 for LSCS) regardless, so the rate differences drive the absorption percentage but not the authorised total.",
