        "summary": "hypothesis=Jyothi Single A/C room + consultant tariff is PAYER-SPECIFIC (Manipal Cigna pays at a 50%-higher rate than NIA/FHPL or Go Digit), NOT temporally drifting. Three observations now anchor this: case_f90295b5e3c2 (May 2025, NIA/FHPL, LSCS): Rs.2,000 + Rs.1,000; case_9222d8c6ffd0 (May-Jun 2025, Manipal Cigna, LSCS): Rs.3,000 + Rs.1,500 (+50%); THIS CASE (May 2025, Go Digit, ENT): Rs.2,000 + Rs.1,000. Both NIA/FHPL and Go Digit see the lower tariff in the same month that Manipal Cigna sees the higher tariff. UPDATES (and falsifies the temporal-rise leg of) the original case_9222d8c6ffd0 §6.7 / Tier-3 e010 hypothesis. Implication for hospital: Jyothi has multi-tariff agreements with different payers — Manipal Cigna's corporate-rate agreement gives a higher per-day room/consultant rate than the standard rates extended to NIA, FHPL, or Go Digit. Recoverable lever: across the remaining 25 folders, identify which payers are on the higher-tariff vs lower-tariff agreement so the Tier-3 cross-payer rate matrix can be built.; tier=3",
